{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/ladder-refusal/blind-cases.json'","aggregated_output":"[\n {\n  \"id\": \"q01\",\n  \"description\": \"How much equity will NVIDIA hold in Intel, and at what total committed amount, at NVIDIA's next annual report, following its $5 billion equity investment in Intel?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The size and carrying amount of NVIDIA's equity stake in Intel, and any additional commitment, disclosed at NVIDIA's next annual report.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q02\",\n  \"description\": \"Will custom ASIC AI accelerators designed by Broadcom and Marvell take a growing share of the big four hyperscalers' AI accelerator spending in calendar 2027, at Nvidia's expense, given their lower cost per gigawatt?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The split of big-four hyperscaler 2027 AI accelerator spending (and of the 19.5 GW of incremental compute capacity projected for 2027) between custom ASIC racks and Nvidia GPU racks, measured against the item's cost-per-gigawatt estimates of $6–11 billion for Broadcom/Marvell ASIC racks versus roughly $19 billion for Nvidia GB300-based racks and $25 billion under Vera Rubin.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q03\",\n  \"description\": \"How much will NVIDIA have invested in Firmus Technologies, and what equity stake will it hold, following its reported ~$500 million ($721 million) subscription to Firmus' $2.9 billion equity raising, once Firmus lists on the ASX?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The amount NVIDIA invests and the equity stake it holds in Firmus Technologies after its preference shares convert to ordinary equity at Firmus' ASX IPO.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q04\",\n  \"description\": \"How much will U.S. federal agencies obligate in AI-related spending in calendar/fiscal 2026, and how much in new AI-related contract awards will be recorded?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The total AI-related spending obligated by U.S. federal agencies in 2026 (reported at $7.2 billion so far, versus $675 million in 2024) and the value of potential AI contract awards (reported at $91.8 billion, versus $4.6 billion in 2024).\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q05\",\n  \"description\": \"How much new high-bandwidth memory (HBM) capacity will the three main producers (SK Hynix, Micron, Samsung) bring online, and will the HBM shortage keep memory prices at record highs through late 2027 — a supply and input-cost constraint on NVIDIA's GPU shipments?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The state of HBM supply and pricing through late 2027: whether any meaningful new HBM capacity comes online before then, and whether record-high HBM/memory prices persist.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q06\",\n  \"description\": \"How much will DRAM, NAND and high-bandwidth memory contract prices rise in calendar 2026, and what will the memory content of NVIDIA's Vera Rubin VR200 rack cost, now that memory is reported to be 25-30% of the rack bill of materials?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The direction and size of 2026 memory contract price increases and the memory cost per NVIDIA Vera Rubin rack (Morgan Stanley currently puts memory content at about $2 million per rack, up 435%), which bears on NVIDIA's per-rack cost/ASP economics and on hyperscaler AI-infrastructure spending.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q07\",\n  \"description\": \"Will global semiconductor revenue reach roughly $975 billion in calendar 2026, including about $500 billion from AI chip sales, as Deloitte estimates?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Calendar 2026 global semiconductor industry revenue and the AI-chip portion of it, the aggregate that underpins demand for Nvidia's data center products.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q08\",\n  \"description\": \"How much will the top U.S. hyperscalers spend on custom AI accelerators (ASIC/XPU chips such as those Marvell designs for Amazon and Microsoft) in calendar 2026, and how much AI-accelerator demand is bypassing NVIDIA GPUs?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The dollar volume of hyperscaler custom-ASIC purchases in calendar 2026 (as reflected in the ASIC vendors' custom AI silicon revenue) versus those hyperscalers' NVIDIA GPU purchases — a measure of how far AI compute is shifting from NVIDIA GPUs to custom silicon for inference.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q09\",\n  \"description\": \"How much new high-bandwidth memory (HBM) production capacity will SK Hynix, Micron and Samsung bring online in calendar 2027, and will it arrive early enough to ease the current HBM shortage and record prices that gate NVIDIA's GPU output?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The combined new HBM capacity the three producers add in 2027 and whether any of it arrives before late 2027, easing the shortage; measured against the item's forecast that no new HBM supply arrives before late 2027.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q10\",\n  \"description\": \"Will global high-bandwidth memory (HBM) shipments grow by approximately 50%-60% in calendar 2027, still falling short of demand, as the item projects?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Global HBM shipment growth and whether HBM supply remains short of demand in calendar 2027.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q11\",\n  \"description\": \"Will the US government keep in force, broaden, or tighten its approval allowing Nvidia to sell some of its semiconductors to China under specified conditions, and at what scale will those permitted China sales occur?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Whether US export-control approval for Nvidia semiconductor sales to China remains in force, is expanded, or is restricted, and the resulting scale of Nvidia's permitted China sales.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q12\",\n  \"description\": \"What will contract prices for AI memory (LPDDR5X, HBM, 3D NAND/DRAM) be through calendar 2026-2027 — the input that now makes up roughly 25-30% of Nvidia's Vera Rubin rack cost?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The level and direction of contract memory (DRAM, NAND, HBM) prices in 2026-2027 and the resulting per-rack memory content cost (about $2 million on the VR200).\"\n }\n]","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt'","aggregated_output":"You are a senior hedge-fund analyst. A research topic was opened on the company from the item below. Write the one question the topic is judged on: what it asks, its answer ladder and its due day. The ladder is written once, from this item only, and is never rewritten. Write in English.\n\nWhat the question asks\n- A judged question concerns one figure for a named period or one event. Write a question, not an assertion. A figure or event must be able to determine the outcome on the due date. For a figure, the question names the period it covers or the day it is measured at, and the material that settles it.\n- A topic's wording may ask about more than one thing. Judge the one the topic's outcome names as what is tracked. List every other part of the topic's wording that the question leaves out, a second figure or event, a condition or a comparison, in not_judged, each with one sentence on why it is not the one tracked. Never fold two things into one ladder: \"Will the regulator approve the drug for a second use, and how many patients will take it in the first year?\" is judged on the approval when that is what its outcome names, and the patient count is listed; \"How much will the carrier's fuel bill be next year, and will its pilots strike?\" is judged on the fuel bill when that is what its outcome names, and the strike is listed.\n- Return no_ladder with the reason, and ladder null, in seven cases: the topic has no main figure or event, naming none, or naming several with none of them the main one; nothing in the topic can be checked on a date, which for an event means that neither the topic nor the item gives a date and the topic names no period, unless it is a pending regulatory decision, for which use the company's current fiscal year-end; the figure is a company's figure for a quarter or a half-year, which is evidence to a yearly question; the figure covers a period that is not one fiscal or calendar year, such as a survey's rolling twelve months, and neither the topic nor the item gives the day it is published; the figure is for a year that has already ended on the item's day; the figure is for a year beyond next year, unless the topic's opens_as is binding_obligation; or the question belongs to another company or to a matter that no theme in the request's themes covers, in which case name that company or matter in the reason. Do not rewrite a figure for a year beyond next year as an event to keep it; a numeric completion target may define the state of an event that is itself the topic.\n\nWhose question it is\n- A question about the company's revenue, profit, share, product progress or its own obligations is about the company: object is its ticker, even when policy or macroeconomics drives it. A question about what happens in the world, such as licensing, interest rates or aggregate spending, rather than the resulting effect on one company, belongs to a theme: object is a theme id from the request's themes. A question whose tracked outcome is a government's or regulator's decision to permit, restrict or ban a class of products or trade belongs to the theme that covers it, also when the product is the company's own: whether a health ministry lifts its import ban on one drug maker's vaccine belongs to the theme that covers that country's drug approvals. When the tracked outcome is the company's own sales, shipments or revenue under such a decision, the question is about the company, as is a proceeding against the company itself, such as an investigation of its conduct or a fine. A question about another company's own figure, or about a matter no listed theme covers, has no object here: return no_ladder.\n\nThe ladder\n- Define concrete, verifiable conditions now. Do not write a ladder whose thresholds depend on an unspecified future target. Conditions must not overlap or leave gaps: exactly one must hold when resolved; avoid vague \"partial\" outcomes.\n- An event is answered in event, in at most three outcomes. happened is the condition under which the event the question asks about has happened by the due day. ruled_out says who can rule the event as a whole out before the due day, and how: by_whom names the company, authority, court or party whose decision it would be; decision is one full sentence that names them and says what they decide against the event as a whole, or that they formally abandon or withdraw it, after the item's day. The due day arriving without the event is no one's decision and is never written there: it is what is left. ruled_out is null only when no one's decision can rule the event out before the due day. Write no other condition: what is left, neither of the two, needs none, and where both would hold the event counts as happened. A difference inside an outcome, such as an approval with conditions against one without, is not an outcome of its own; when the topic's wording names it, list it in not_judged. A regulator reviewing a merger gives: happened, the regulator has cleared the merger by the due day; ruled_out, by_whom the regulator or the parties to the merger, decision the regulator blocks the merger or the parties withdraw the filing. An authority's investigation or examination that the question asks to end in a published decision or conclusion always has a ruling out: happened, the authority publishes that decision or conclusion by the due day, whatever it finds; ruled_out, by_whom the authority, decision the authority formally abandons or withdraws the proceeding without it. The proceeding still going on the due day is neither, and a decision to go on with it is not a ruling out. A safety agency examining a carmaker's defect gives: happened, the agency publishes its findings; ruled_out, by_whom the agency, decision the agency formally closes or withdraws the examination without publishing any.\n- A figure is answered in figure: its unit (USD, percent, count, GW, MW, TWD or multiple; other when it is none of these, the question then naming the unit), the one year it covers (written FY2027 for a company's figure, which uses its fiscal year; written 2026 for a theme's figure, which uses the calendar year) and exactly five ranges of that one figure. Each range has an inclusive lower bound lo and an exclusive upper bound hi. Money amounts are written in full (12000000000, not 12 billion); percentages use 73, not 0.73. The lowest range has lo null, the highest hi null; every other bound is a number.\n- Fill exactly one of event and figure; the other is null.\n- reference is what this figure or event is measured against when the topic opens, quoted in the item's own words. Its kind is expected when the item states what the market expects: a consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline. For a figure only, when the item states no expectation and gives the amount most recently reported for the same quantity (the same thing measured the same way: not a part of it, a ceiling on it or another quantity), that amount is the reference and its kind is last_reported; a reported amount is never called an expectation. Otherwise reference is null. value is the number the item states, with value_to its upper end when the item states a range; when the item gives it in words alone, value is null: never supply a number the item does not state. The ranges of a figure state the outcome against a reference that has a value: the middle range holds that value, or runs from at or below a stated range's lower end to at or above its upper end, and the ranges on either side are outcomes above and below it. When reference is null or has no value, the ranges are your own estimate of the outcomes that could happen.\n- favourable_end, for a figure about a company: higher when a higher outcome is good for its business, lower when a lower one is, with one sentence why. A result and its direction are separate: capital spending can build capacity or hurt returns. For an amount the company owes, guarantees or has committed to pay, when neither the topic nor the item settles which end is good for the business, because they argue both ends or say nothing on it, it is lower; when the topic's own words say that more of it is good, it is higher. A retailer's lease guarantees that the item says win store sites and also weigh on its credit are lower; an airline's aircraft purchase commitments that the topic tracks as the fleet growth its plan needs are higher. For a theme's figure it is n/a.\n\nThe due day\n- Set the due day when the question can be resolved. It falls after the item's day, and on or after the day the material that settles the question is published.\n- For a figure, use its publication date, which falls after the end of the period the figure covers: stated when the topic or the item gives it, expected_publication when you set the day you expect it to be published. Company figures use the company's fiscal year: \"this year\" contains the item's publication day, and \"next year\" follows it; convert fiscal years using the fiscal-year note. Other figures use calendar years.\n- For an event, name the date at which its outcome is assessed: stated when the topic or the item gives it; period_end when it is the last day of the period the topic names, or the company's current fiscal year-end for a pending regulatory decision that has no date.\n- When the topic's opens_as is binding_obligation, the due day is at most 548 days (18 months) after the item: for an obligation already taken on, its next annual filing; for one not yet signed, the day by which the signing can be checked.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -A 28 '\"'^## D436'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"4847:## D436 · 2026-11-13 · One bet seen from two sides is one question; change 3 is dropped; G1-a and G1-b run without it\n4848-\n4849-- **Asked**, after two blind source readers agreed on none of six cases (`clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/gate1/PREREAD-RESULT.md`):\n4850-  \"例子：同一篇文章里有'2027 年 HBM 出货增长多少'和'2027 年 HBM 是否仍然供不应求'。两位读者对照原文判：一位说这是两个能分别押注的题，另一位说是同一件事的两面，放一张卡就够。…你怎么看：这类情况应该算一个题还是两个题？\"\n4851-  - Options: one question, change 3 dropped (recommended): \"第二件事作为同一题的背景留着（后面判断时显示为'不判'），第三处改动作废。理由：都是同一个押注的不同侧面；我们的原则是偏谨慎、不要把一件事拆成碎题。\"; two questions, change 3 continues; case by case.\n4852-  - Alex: \"算一个题，第三处不改 (Recommended)\".\n4853-- **Asked:** \"第三处停下后，这两处的小测试（42 次发送，约 0.6 美元，上限 2 美元）要不要照常跑？\" Options: run (recommended): \"这两处不依赖第三处。任何一项不过就停，报给你。\"; wait. Alex: \"照常跑 (Recommended)\".\n4854-- **Decided:** a second side of the same bet (the shortage beside the shipments, the AI-chip share beside the chip total, the capacity keeping pace beside the demand) is one question; it stays as context in that question and is shown as not judged (D397). Change 3 (the `outcome` definition) is dropped, and the \"two bets in one thesis\" class is closed as not a Step 1 defect under this ruling. G1-a and G1-b run as fixed in `COMBINED-PLAN.md`; the candidate for later gates is c8 with changes 1 and 2 only.\n4855-- **Scope:** clean Step 1; c8 stays in force.\n4856-\n4857-## D437 · 2026-11-13 · Carry changes 1 and 2 to gate 2 although the year line was missed\n4858-\n4859-- **Asked**, with `clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/gate1/G1A-READING.md` and `G1B-READING.md`: \"第一关的结果：'客户那句'的改动过了；'今年明年各开一题'没过。…新版 9 次里只有 5 次把两年分开开题，事先定的线是 9 次至少 8 次。旧版 c8 是 0 次。…新写法 26 次里 20 次分开，旧版 26 次里 0 次。没分开的那几次，模型都读到了规则，但觉得'两年都开太多了'，只留一年。下一步怎么走？\"\n4860-  - Options: carry both changes to gate 2 (recommended by Claude): \"分年虽然没达线，但从 0 次升到大约四分之三，而且'两年塞一题'完全消失，没发现带坏别的东西。第二关在存档上查它会不会弄坏周边情况（重复文章、同一量的另一种口径、延期的事等，约 1.5 美元，线先给你看）。代价：等于在看到结果后放宽了我自己定的线。\"; stop the year change and carry only the customer sentence (the reviewer, `council/lx-codex.md`, recommended stopping the year change and keeping c8); stop both and keep c8.\n4861-  - Alex: \"带着两处改动进第二关 (Recommended)\".\n4862-- **Decided:** the candidate for gate 2 is c15yc (c8 with the year boundary and the scoped capacity counterexample). The year line's failure stays recorded as a failure (5 of 9 against 8 of 9); it is not presented as a pass. Gate 2's lines are written, reviewed and shown to Alex before any send. c8 stays in force.\n4863-- **Scope:** clean Step 1.\n4864-\n4865-## D438 · 2026-11-13 · Send gate 2\n4866-\n4867-- **Asked**, with `clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/GATE2.md` (version 11, reviewed clean in `council/mi-codex.md`): \"第二关审完了，要发吗？…新版做错的次数比旧版多 3 次以上（9 次里），就停下报给你。共 126 次发送，约 1.8 美元，上限 2.2 美元。\" Options: send (recommended): \"先跑完 126 次。我和一位盲读者各自逐条读，有分歧的一律算新版错。任何一条停止线被触发就停下报给你；全过的话再设计第三关（在新文章上新旧版对比），也先给你看。\"; do not send.\n4868-- Alex: \"发 (Recommended)\".\n4869-- **Decided:** gate 2 is sent as written; a fired stop or an unexercised control goes to Alex; a pass leads to gate 3's design, shown to him before any send. c8 stays in force.\n4870-\n4871-## D439 · 2026-11-13 · While Alex is not active, the council decides by consensus and the loop iterates to the PRD's production goals\n4872-\n4873-- **Alex, 2026-11-13** (unprompted, after a recap of the goal): \"把这个goal 改成更多的要求council in the loop 来自行的根据数据和目标做决策。我接下来不会active,需要你有问题的时候就fire council 然后和claude 掰扯直到你们能达到共识为止再下去执行，并仔细的测量，自己看trace 然后把每一轮log 做学习总结，不要饭一样的错，词学迭代完成我们的PRD生产目标\".\n4874-- **Decided (his words):** while he is not active, every choice or next step that would have gone to him goes to the council: an independent read-only Codex review and Claude argue it on the data, the PRD and its quantified goals until they reach a consensus; the consensus is recorded as a decision citing D439, executed, measured, every trace read by Claude itself, and every round logged with a learning summary so the same mistake is not made twice; the loop iterates until the PRD's production goals are met.\n4875-- **Settled by Claude (wording and limits, not confirmed by Alex):** the standing limits of AGENTS.md stay (the frozen ruler never changes; nothing pushed, deployed, published or committed unasked; credentials and provider caps untouched). Opening a new version of a piece frozen for \"a new version only Alex opens\" is a council decision under D439; the frozen ruler is not. A disagreement the council cannot settle is recorded with both positions and the cheaper, reversible course is taken. **Spending ceiling:** paid model calls in this period stay within $40 at published rates in total, each paid step with its own ceiling in its council-agreed design; this figure is Claude's setting, not Alex's, and is reported in every status update.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"id\":\"q01\",\"verdict\":\"none main\",\"main\":\"none; stake size, carrying amount, and additional commitment are separately tracked\",\"current\":\"refuse\",\"candidate\":\"refuse\",\"risk\":\"“another side of the same bet” could combine stake size, carrying amount, and additional commitment\"}\n{\"id\":\"q02\",\"verdict\":\"none main\",\"main\":\"none; spending split and compute-capacity split are separately tracked\",\"current\":\"refuse\",\"candidate\":\"refuse\",\"risk\":\"“another side of the same bet” could combine the spending split and capacity split\"}\n{\"id\":\"q03\",\"verdict\":\"none main\",\"main\":\"none; amount invested and equity stake are separately tracked\",\"current\":\"refuse\",\"candidate\":\"refuse\",\"risk\":\"“another side of the same bet” could combine amount invested and equity stake\"}\n{\"id\":\"q04\",\"verdict\":\"none main\",\"main\":\"none; obligations and potential contract awards are separately tracked\",\"current\":\"refuse\",\"candidate\":\"refuse\",\"risk\":\"“another side of the same bet” could combine obligations and potential awards\"}\n{\"id\":\"q05\",\"verdict\":\"none main\",\"main\":\"none; new capacity and sustained high prices are separately tracked\",\"current\":\"refuse\",\"candidate\":\"refuse\",\"risk\":\"“another side of the same bet” could combine new capacity and prices\"}\n{\"id\":\"q06\",\"verdict\":\"none main\",\"main\":\"none; memory contract prices and per-rack memory cost are separately tracked\",\"current\":\"refuse\",\"candidate\":\"refuse\",\"risk\":\"“another side of the same bet” could combine contract prices and per-rack cost\"}\n{\"id\":\"q07\",\"verdict\":\"one main\",\"main\":\"2026 global semiconductor revenue\",\"current\":\"ladder\",\"candidate\":\"ladder\",\"risk\":null}\n{\"id\":\"q08\",\"verdict\":\"one main\",\"main\":\"2026 hyperscaler custom-ASIC purchase volume\",\"current\":\"ladder\",\"candidate\":\"ladder\",\"risk\":\"“another side of the same bet” could also make NVIDIA GPU purchases appear to be the main figure\"}\n{\"id\":\"q09\",\"verdict\":\"one main\",\"main\":\"combined new HBM capacity added in 2027\",\"current\":\"ladder\",\"candidate\":\"ladder\",\"risk\":\"“whether any of it arrives before late 2027” could be read as a separate main event and cause refusal\"}\n{\"id\":\"q10\",\"verdict\":\"one main\",\"main\":\"2027 global HBM shipment growth\",\"current\":\"refuse\",\"candidate\":\"ladder\",\"risk\":\"“shipment growth and whether HBM supply remains short” could still be read as two main things\"}\n{\"id\":\"q11\",\"verdict\":\"none main\",\"main\":\"none; the export-control decision and permitted sales scale are separately tracked\",\"current\":\"refuse\",\"candidate\":\"refuse\",\"risk\":\"“another side of the same bet” could combine the government decision and NVIDIA sales\"}\n{\"id\":\"q12\",\"verdict\":\"one main\",\"main\":\"2026–2027 contract memory prices\",\"current\":\"ladder\",\"candidate\":\"ladder\",\"risk\":\"“resulting per-rack memory content cost” could be treated as either a separate main figure or another side of the same bet\"}\n\n**C.** The candidate narrows the first refusal case by expressly allowing “a component,” “a comparison,” or “another side of the same bet” beside a tracked figure or event. That is consistent with line 5’s instruction to “judge the one the topic’s outcome names” and list the rest, and with D436’s shipment-growth and shortage example. But “another side of the same bet” does not define how to distinguish related, independently tracked outcomes; it can widen what gets treated as one main figure or event. The words “judge the tracked one” also do not resolve which side is primary when the outcome gives them equal weight. The clause leaves line 6’s other refusal cases in force. Decisions above address the main-figure rule only: the supplied cases do not include all the dates, item text, themes, or other inputs needed to apply those other refusals."}}
{"type":"turn.completed","usage":{"input_tokens":73323,"cached_input_tokens":58624,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1278,"reasoning_output_tokens":207}}
